
extract_allele_kmers.pl

This script generates allele-centered k-mers from a reference genome and a VCF-like variant stream. It is a utility used to support downstream Korus workflows by producing fixed-length sequence embeddings for both reference and alternate alleles at each variant site.

Purpose
-------
extract_allele_kmers.pl converts variant representations (SNVs and small INDELs) into k-mer embeddings centered on the variant position, enabling downstream comparison against sample-specific k-mer profiles (e.g., Bloom filter–based genotyping or similarity scoring).

Unlike traditional SNV-only extractors, this implementation supports:

SNVs
insertions
deletions
multi-allelic sites (multiple ALT representations per position)

Each allele is embedded independently in a fixed-length k-mer window anchored at the variant position.

Inputs
------
The script takes two positional arguments:

extract_allele_kmers.pl <reference.fa.gz> <k>

reference.fa.gz : Indexed or gzipped reference genome (FASTA format)
k : k-mer length (must be odd for symmetric centering; e.g., 45, 55, 75)

Variant records are read from STDIN in tab-delimited VCF-like format:

CHROM  POS  ID  REF  ALT  ...

Multi-allelic ALT fields are supported via comma separation.

Output
------
For each variant site, the script emits:

CHROM  POS  REF  <REF_kmer>
CHROM  POS  ALT  <ALT_kmer>
One REF k-mer per site (anchored at the reference allele)
One or more ALT k-mers per site (one per alternate allele representation)
All k-mers are fixed length k

Key Properties
--------------
Fixed-length embedding: All outputs are length k, regardless of INDEL size
Reference-anchored centering: Variants are embedded using a centered genomic window
Multi-allelic aware: Multiple ALT representations per locus are preserved
Genome-consistent refill: INDEL-induced gaps are filled from the reference genome to maintain coordinate consistency
Streaming design: Operates on STDIN VCF-like streams for pipeline integration

Notes / Design Assumptions
--------------------------
The script assumes variants are already left-normalized (as in standard VCF pipelines).
REF validation is performed against the reference genome slice at the center of the k-mer window.
Multi-ALT sites are treated independently; downstream tools are responsible for aggregation or collapsing allele redundancy.
Output is designed for compatibility with Bloom filter–based k-mer querying workflows used in Korus.

Example
-------

cat variants.vcf \
  | grep -v '^#' \
  | perl tools/extract_allele_kmers.pl GRCh38.fa.gz 45 \
  > allele_kmers.tsv

Role in Korus pipeline
----------------------
This script is not part of the core Korus inference engine, but serves as a preprocessing utility that converts variant call representations into a k-mer space suitable for downstream KorusMatrix construction and sample-level signal aggregation.

